{title: What Child Is This}
{artist: William Chatterton Dix / Greensleeves}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Carol}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 6/8}
{score: what-child-is-this.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
What [Em]child is [D]this, who [B7]laid to [Em]rest
On [G]Mary's [D]lap is [B7]sleeping
Whom [Em]angels [D]greet with [B7]anthems [Em]sweet
While [G]shepherds [D]watch are [B7]keeping
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
This, [G]this is [D]Christ the [Em]King
Whom [Am]shepherds [B7]guard and [Em]angels sing
Haste, [G]haste to [D]bring Him [Em]laud
The [Am]babe, the [B7]son of [Em]Mary
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Why [Em]lies He [D]in such [B7]mean es[Em]tate
Where [G]ox and [D]ass are [B7]feeding
Good [Em]Christian, [D]fear, for [B7]sinners [Em]here
The [G]silent [D]Word is [B7]pleading
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
So [Em]bring Him [D]incense, [B7]gold and [Em]myrrh
Come [G]peasant, [D]king to [B7]own Him
The [Em]King of [D]kings sal[B7]vation [Em]brings
Let [G]loving [D]hearts en[B7]throne Him
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
